# =============================================================================
# portainer/.env  —  copy to .env and edit
# =============================================================================

# Hostname for the Portainer UI. Required — compose refuses to start without
# it rather than routing on an empty Host rule.
#
# Used twice: the Traefik router rule, and Portainer's --trusted-origins CSRF
# allowlist. They must be the same value, which is why it is one variable.
#
# BARE HOSTNAME. No scheme, no trailing slash, no port. Portainer exits with
# "invalid url for trusted origin" on any of those.
PORTAINER_DOMAIN=portainer.example.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT here: the admin password and the DB encryption key.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are file secrets under ./secrets/, so they never appear in
# `docker inspect` or `docker compose config`.
#
#   make init
#
# The encryption key is generated for you. Back it up — an encrypted store
# without its key does not open, and there is no recovery.
